.TH hello-lisp "1" "September 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI Hello Command"
.SH NAME
hello-lisp \- Print a greeting and a fresh UUID using a Common Lisp script
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hello-lisp
.RI [ EXIT_CODE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B hello-lisp
is a minimal example command that runs a Common Lisp script with
.BR sbcl (1)
from the
.I lib/cl/
directory of the SMI toolset installation.
It demonstrates that Common Lisp scripting is correctly set up: SBCL is on the PATH, the SMI
library location is resolvable, and Quicklisp can load libraries.
.PP
The script loads the
.B cl-uuid
library (system name
.BR uuid )
through Quicklisp and prints a greeting naming the current working directory and a fresh
version 4 UUID.
On the first run Quicklisp downloads the library; every later run uses the already compiled
local copy, so only the first run needs network access.
.PP
Quicklisp must be set up for the user first, see
.BR quicklisp-setup (1)
and
.BR quicklisp-user-setup (1):
the script loads
.IR ~/quicklisp/setup.lisp ,
because
.B sbcl --script
does not read
.IR ~/.sbclrc .
.PP
The command mirrors
.BR hello-elixir (1)
one to one, exit code handling included, so the same program can be compared across the two
languages.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I EXIT_CODE
Optional integer to exit with, in the range
.B 0
to
.BR 255 ,
the range a POSIX shell can report as the status of a command.
Defaults to
.B 0
when omitted.
An argument that is not an integer, or that falls outside that range, is rejected and the
command exits
.BR 1 .
A non-zero exit code is echoed before exiting; further arguments are ignored.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, or no
.I EXIT_CODE
argument was given.
.TP
.B 1
The
.I EXIT_CODE
argument was not an integer in the range
.B 0
to
.BR 255 .
.TP
.I EXIT_CODE
The value passed on the command line, when valid.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $(smi-lib-location)/cl/hello-lisp.lisp
The Common Lisp script executed by this command.
.TP
.I ~/quicklisp/
Quicklisp installation and library cache.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sbcl (1),
.BR hello-elixir (1),
.BR quicklisp-setup (1),
.BR quicklisp-user-setup (1),
.BR smi-lib-location (1)
